Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.0  Introduction", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"2b324f19-b4f9-480b-a233-3efa58047f54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "This package allows calculations in Riemannian Geometry by defining all \
basic tensors and tensor operations. Tensors are represented as nested lists \
of their components in a particular frame (default = coordinate frame). \
Functions are defined for Raising/Lowering indices, Contracting (multiple) \
indices on one (or between two) tensors, for Covariant and Lie \
Differentiation and for classifying the Weyl and Ricci tensors. One can also \
use standard ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " functions like ",
 StyleBox["Dot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Outer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (giving tensor products), and ",
 StyleBox["Transpose",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (index rearrangement) to create new (lists representing) tensors. "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"4c8972a6-079f-4079-9879-4b2f18827fb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tGiven a metric and a set of coordinates, the main routine in the package \
computes explicit expressions for all common Riemannian Geometry tensors \
(Riemann, Ricci, Einstein, Weyl) and tests if the space belongs to any of the \
following categories: ",
 StyleBox["Flat",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Conformally Flat",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Ricci Flat",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Einstein Space",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Space of Constant Curvature",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Each tensor is stored as a nested list under an appropriate global name. \
One can optionally specify a frame (if different from the coordinate frame) \
with respect to which tensor components are to be computed. "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"69fb5a1d-8a3a-460d-9255-7d430e99623f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8e4e2d16-e356-49f4-a4d7-0562ee64125a"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"11d8edbd-1893-4f70-a064-7e3c4ef6567e"],
 "\tThe Riemann and Ricci tensor sign conventions used are:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", 
    RowBox[{"b", ";", "c", ";", "d"}]],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ca7cc13a-0049-43b3-a574-3780e94d32d5"],
 " - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", 
    RowBox[{"b", ";", "d", ";", "c"}]],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"68eeb83b-9474-48d4-b052-c8618385b70f"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["V", "a"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a74cce34-12b7-4ff0-9966-25fca1f673fe"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontSize->12],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "bcd"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"34caa812-7952-4b34-9beb-070f7d01ac4b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["R", "ab"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "edc13696-b30c-407e-97e1-bbdb2c1dd573"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "s"], "asb"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"26c8710f-10db-48f8-a5c9-2df7b935b8cb"],
 ", so that Einstein's equations are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["R", "ab"], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", "2"], "R", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["g", "ab"]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"+", "\[Kappa]"}], " ", 
    SubscriptBox["T", "ab"]}]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d80cce7c-2262-47e7-93a3-0ba07ecea3f9"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Kappa]", "=", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", "\[Pi]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"G", "/", 
     SuperscriptBox["c", "4"]}]}]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c940e74b-f682-4ffe-845e-0606a8c5284e"],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"2c670a48-25e0-4fd7-9369-054957ac0082"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.1  Basic Input /Output & Notation", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"6caee4e7-dbdf-4e38-bac3-2e8699d611ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "To define the geometry, begin by computing all basic Riemannian Geometry \
tensors for a particular metric. To do this:\n",
 StyleBox["\t ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(0) In a new notebook, evaluate the initialization code: ",
 StyleBox["<<EDCRGTCcode.m",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\t (1) Define a list symbols (coordinate names) and give it a name -- say \
",
 StyleBox["xIN",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->18,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["=",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->18],
 StyleBox["{t,r,\[Theta],\[Phi]};",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n\t (2) Define a symmetric matrix (list of lists) of functions of the \
coordinates (the metric) and give it a name -- say \n",
 StyleBox["gIN",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["={{1-2M/r,0,0,0},{0,-1/(1-2M/r),0,0},{0,0,-r^2,0},{0,0,0,-(r^2 \
Sin[\[Theta]]^2)}};",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n\t(3) Assign appropriate simplification rules to the global list ",
 StyleBox["simpRules",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->18,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " as needed (see Examples and Usage Tips). For example: ",
 StyleBox["simpRules={",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "->", "1"}],
   FontFamily->"Courier"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9f8be087-7df0-4e0b-8439-539fd8c0e8cc"],
 StyleBox["};",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n\t(4) Evaluate ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors[gIN,xIN]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->18,
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"5f209b81-a7b6-4560-967c-b30ccadb1815"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["RGtensors",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  computes all common Riemannian Geometry tensors, printing messages along \
the way. It also tests if the space is ",
 StyleBox["Flat,",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["Conformally Flat",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Ricci Flat",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Einstein Space",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Space of Constant Curvature",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and, if yes, prints corresponding messages. When it is finished, the \
following \"tensors\" -- nested lists -- are stored in memory and can be used \
in further calculations (the letters U, d  in the tensor names serve as \
mnemonic devices for the position -- ",
 StyleBox["Up",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["down",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " -- of the relevant indices) :"
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"68bf135f-0e63-4ca9-9f3a-6c16c774fa8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["gdd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (covariant form of the metric tensor), with components gdd[[a,b]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["g", "ab"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5c370781-9274-472c-8bce-7aec3ed44944"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"18e13e01-555f-4c6e-91cb-19935052484f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["gUU",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (contravariant form of the metric tensor), with components gUU[[a,b]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["g", "ab"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "de728131-b198-4a5e-8696-7e87354f23ee"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"47be14e5-260f-41b5-bd36-4ab48f10f48d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["GUdd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (Christoffel symbols of the 2nd kind), with components GUdd[[a,b,c]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "bc", "a"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e769a8ce-423a-4b09-a23a-0a97212271fa"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"9f05d15d-1a7e-4ab6-b139-6ec1544670f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Rdddd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (covariant form of the Riemann tensor), with components Rdddd[[a,b,c,d]] = \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox["R", "abcd"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"f6931190-40eb-4ada-b952-e99ec7874e3a"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"3780f30b-e153-437d-89b3-3ed073daf029"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["RUddd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (mixed form of the Riemann tensor), with components RUddd[[a,b,c,d]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "bcd"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"419e28e7-36c4-4886-95e0-39a67cc3c9be"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"1b41e437-9be5-455f-bfe6-7014cd463f88"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"112bbba7-4e30-42b8-bb0a-7e51d74b039a"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Rdd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (covariant form of the Ricci tensor), with components Rdd[[a,b]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["R", "ab"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7527250a-ffdb-4c74-a2b9-69102e6bfe7c"],
 " \[Congruent] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "s"], "asb"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"20d8ee07-6a99-4939-ba37-b9ae3acb1b44"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"9972d9ed-e4c5-4de4-9df0-cbaf8f52e1bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["EUd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (mixed form of the Einstein tensor), with components EUd[[a,b]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["E", "a"], "b"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"4872f340-1140-43e1-a8b5-397b610de8ae"],
 " \[Congruent] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "b"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8ca874c9-3193-4971-b9c4-291f3443d37e"],
 "- ",
 StyleBox["R/2",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"], "b"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d83ab06b-0ef7-408b-aeb8-1543f69ecb38"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"eedf1b2b-5ac2-4884-b9c3-b5aa3ec0ccab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"11bff91c-3478-4f8d-bcdb-e2032d9a1b28"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"9f565c53-25f7-4a6a-8154-baff152bc7a1"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is the curvature scalar    (",
 StyleBox["Important: Do not use the symbol R in coordinates or metric!",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ")"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"2bb2efa8-a043-4f9c-8043-0e2250e5bea7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Wdddd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (covariant form of the Weyl tensor), with components Wdddd[[a,b,c,d]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "abcd"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a70093fc-f959-4b66-a9a1-c74d79f000fa"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"ac57db93-a796-4e9c-8bca-ae7433ded89f"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"73866271-6541-45b0-b680-3fdfdfcc56cd"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"5dbfdcb7-1391-4df5-a249-1d4039ef5db3"],
 "\tFinally, ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " defines the following global variables: (i) ",
 StyleBox["coordList",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " contains the coordinates defined in (1) above, (ii) ",
 StyleBox["detg",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is the determinant of the metric, (iii) ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " stores the dimension of the space and (iv) ",
 StyleBox["LineElement",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " stores, of course, the line element! Tensor components refer to the \
coordinate frame and are numbered ",
 StyleBox["1,...,Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", rather than ",
 StyleBox["0,...,Dim-1",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", so that the {i,j...k} component of a tensor is the [[i,j...k]] part of \
the corresponding nested list. See section 5, \"",
 StyleBox["Calculating Tensor Components in an Arbitrary Frame",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\", on how to do calculations in an arbitrary frame. "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"e5b3baba-41da-4518-bcf3-2096c7e90d85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"c1c228a5-c8a8-41f9-a6be-0871139f664c"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"716c70a1-c6a1-4008-a25e-e3f7b3584001"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": One can choose to skip the most time consuming computations: RUddd, Wdddd \
or EUd. This can be achieved by calling ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  with an optional extra argument -- a list of three numbers ",
 StyleBox["{i,j,k}",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". When the first number is 0, RUddd is not computed; when the second number \
is 0, Wdddd is not computed; and when the third number is 0, EUd is not \
computed. Thus ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors[gIN,xIN,{1,0,0}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  will compute RUddd but not Wdddd or EUd (See Examples 7 and 8). ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " prints warning messages when some tensors are not computed. When EUd is \
not computed, the tests for ",
 StyleBox["Einstein Space",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Space of Constant Curvature",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " are not performed. For compatibility with previous versions of RGTC, the \
optional extra argument can consist of only two numbers corresponding to \
RUddd and Wdddd. Thus ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors[gIN,xIN,{1,0}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is equivalent to ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors[gIN,xIN,{1,0,1}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"0d551833-618c-413f-b08d-64e5e8b7137e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\t1.1.1  Totally antisymmetric symbol / tensor", "Subsubsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"0e534907-8848-4087-bfa8-a7b970096715"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d1ce9ae3-d050-4c3c-b99d-c09b7330009d"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d68aa92e-3d0c-4502-b972-900ea8e0c393"],
 "\t Definitions for the totally antisymmetric symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a1", "..."}], "an"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54ab0df6-130d-43b8-be5e-78e8645783ff"],
 " and tensor  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a1", "..."}], "an"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6ebc5fa0-a844-4361-93d7-731b2c95a671"],
 " are provided, but the tensor is not evaluated unless called by the user. \
As the number of indices on these objects equals the dimension of the \
mannifold, the U/d notation cannot be used. Instead, the following global \
names are used:"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"a59513f9-7c51-4b43-a546-e76fce43ae08"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d0ed674b-7269-4f9f-9972-4b3434371662"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"08052899-6070-4301-a8fd-d07a18b4d295"],
 "\t ",
 StyleBox["epsilon",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a ",
 StyleBox["function",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that takes ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " integers as arguments and returns one of { 0, 1, -1} - the sign of the \
permutation of the arguments. For example, in 5 dimensions,"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"3e4b7901-2c3d-405e-ae78-271120c697a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["epsilon[1,2,3,4,5]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "returns 1,  ",
 StyleBox["epsilon[1,3,2,4,5]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "returns -1, and  ",
 StyleBox["epsilon[1,2,2,4,5]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "returns 0."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"719c43b6-1ad9-4a4f-845d-c6f829573e51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e4505245-2fc2-4495-87b0-8abe0e37d55b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8148ec8a-bf70-4a52-80f0-18f8a7f13e51"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["eta[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " can take 0 to ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " arguments and returns the ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "-rank antisymmetric tensor with raised indices at the position(s) indicated \
by the argument(s). Thus ",
 StyleBox["eta[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is the totally covariant antisymmetric tensor, with components"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"9a81196d-fdbf-46dd-8263-bec2986157c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"69a6a545-44d8-4dde-9fc3-116fb855407b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"dc994884-2389-429b-a9d4-189805ccc21c"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["eta[][[a1,a2,...,an]]=",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", "detg", "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], ")"}], 
   
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf0cde8-a37f-4910-a085-b57271dd99d5"],
 StyleBox["epsilon[a1,a2,...,an]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"1d378a62-742f-4d30-b712-622170e94e08"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b3f44843-a638-4767-bbbb-beeb7e73eaae"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b1fd23be-45d3-43e9-8d24-9a1a39aa66b2"],
 "while"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"932ceba4-13ce-4423-99df-dabfee9f8d76"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"7fd3b7eb-659a-47c9-9a67-8a45c4fe0a3d"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b9d3a111-4b0f-432b-a06e-af876cd7894e"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["eta[2,3][[a1,a2,...,an]]=",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", "detg", "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"a2", " ", "b2"}]]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3c229198-ed0a-425e-a7bd-265d95feaa63"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["g", 
   RowBox[{"a3", " ", "b3"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5caa6ce4-86b7-4e09-8608-945a8a0f9ddf"],
 StyleBox["epsilon[a1,b2,b3,..,an]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"56e76f6b-150d-4644-bc65-3d2eb67e69eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ee6a1415-5998-4dc0-b511-11d856559001"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b0c90c67-2e3d-4428-8e87-26d4e1015428"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Warning",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The evaluation of ",
 StyleBox["eta[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " tensors (",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "-fold nested lists) is ",
 StyleBox["very",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " time consuming in high dimensions as the number of components grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["Dim", "Dim"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "da39a714-ef14-45a3-9229-63b379c2931b"],
 ". It also requires large amounts of memory. For example, for the simple \
case of a conformally flat metric, the {Time, Storage} requirements for \
computing ",
 StyleBox["each",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["eta[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " grow as follows: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"9ca4cd38-28f0-4a65-b7df-76c2019b55ad"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"24c05a1c-406e-44cf-bb39-603352a1caa7"],
 "{~1 sec, <1 MB} for ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "=6, {~20 sec, ~7 MB} for ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "=7, and {> 10 min, >120 MB} for ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "=8! Thus, calculations with ",
 StyleBox["eta[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " should not be attempted if ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ">7. Fortunately, for ",
 StyleBox["Dim",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "=4 the requirements are quite modest, even for complicated metrics."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"feb250c6-0dc5-4864-af65-c9721ed52b1a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"0e0ede58-a07f-42ad-9d91-c5048752b455"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b0529de6-f9d9-402e-a098-d0a29503161b"],
 "\tOnce the basic tensors have been computed, one can use the functions \
defined in the following sections to perform further calculations."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"4c2f5789-22bd-4eeb-b883-c6b8022c1d81"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.2  Manipulation of tensor indices & tensor products", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"68d12292-51e5-4176-a124-fe361bc980eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tThe ",
 StyleBox["first",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["last",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " index of a tensor can be raised / lowered by inner (",
 StyleBox["Dot",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ") multiplication with gUU / gdd:"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"cb46d9f3-1b39-4412-80a0-4da3d42a81f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["Edd=gdd.EUd",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " has components Edd[[a,b]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["E", "ab"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c94fb3ac-2055-4256-be7c-702d2a95e288"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"3f1b374e-6f88-4b08-92d5-d6fb9cb9e33b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["WdddU=Wdddd.gUU",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " has components WdddU[[a,b,c,d]] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["W", "abc"], "d"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e426fc08-374c-4e8f-a198-ed75ae51e1bf"],
 ".",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"f94defc6-49ed-4a53-9cd6-4b421745fceb"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"39063825-66a8-4f7c-b89d-e35dce99956e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"67d0a63c-3a0a-4f5f-8f13-9914ccf2cf9a"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"03de61d2-a047-4fc4-a00d-cf67c0b1dee2"],
 "\tTo manipulate other indices the following functions have been defined:"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"0bc7bd6b-01dd-4b4d-8032-8692f1a93dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"32339c03-a7fa-4f7d-96c9-75f724a994e2"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"bf661c03-ea9f-44db-bf1a-f84c7d02908b"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["Lower[x_,ni__]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ":: lowers the index (indices) at position(s) ",
 StyleBox["ni",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (assumed U) of the nested list ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " using the matrix  gdd."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"bc68b52f-2e6d-44eb-a1c7-8e558ad6ad0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"2f2af690-f009-4209-bed4-f6ad264bb3e0"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d7df2d5a-1f87-42c6-bc5f-9b09713d5401"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["Raise[x_,ni__]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ":: raises the index (indices) at position(s) ",
 StyleBox["ni",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (assumed d) of the nested list ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " using the matrix  gUU."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"b54ebef1-ad6d-4874-ab4c-1bea8720758d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"6b6ed11d-10b0-43cf-a898-3235ac6fe812"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"0a280931-3280-4259-a1d6-d14b0809e9de"],
 "\tFor example, the mixed Riemann tensor with  components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "b"], "c"], "d"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "44371698-16ed-4203-b223-00c4f87a8ab6"],
 "  is  ",
 StyleBox["RUdUd=Raise[RUddd,3]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"4aa210e3-30ae-4326-bfec-1a29723241d6"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"6cf77aea-b6bc-486a-9ea2-81d1f41eaa62"],
 "while  RUUUd",
 StyleBox["=Raise[RUddd,2,3]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  has components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "abc"], "d"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "af7ac6e7-7b61-4fde-8b01-4fe9c935edf1"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"071cc2a5-0ff5-4ded-8469-db6a193a7be3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"a26fe32b-6b43-429f-98c8-ff6d2de96c1b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8bcdf1c0-e15e-4a4a-9bf9-0bd0048790c9"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The functions ",
 StyleBox["Raise",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " / ",
 StyleBox["Lower",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " apply the rules in ",
 StyleBox["simpRules",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and factor the expressions obtained. Thus ",
 StyleBox["Raise[RUddd,4]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is equivalent but not identical to ",
 StyleBox["RUddd.gUU",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"eb136a01-5be6-478e-9ec4-0fb532bf3ac5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"72855f31-c1d0-4bf1-8988-ca466af96223"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"3c962fe9-a1fe-4d4c-8cf7-041900838ecd"],
 "\tTensor products are obtained by using the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " function ",
 StyleBox["Outer",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". For example,"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"ead68687-1dca-46f1-9cff-56896a36c7fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d53a4193-6263-4d03-87ce-4a815adb33b7"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"994d5210-463d-49c9-8eea-a07d8cd9e630"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["gg=Outer[Times,gdd,gdd];",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 4th rank (d-type) tensor with components ",
 StyleBox["gg[[a,b,c,d]]=",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   SubscriptBox["g", "ab"]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"fe7b8d4f-745a-4c73-bf56-c67252a3b197"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["g", "cd"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"e0ab3042-9354-47f7-bc0b-6716beddea47"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"e83236e5-8e85-4017-88eb-8a07932b83a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ba0d4ac9-f630-4330-9436-6ab29204771e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"21d9f127-6f56-4cbd-be90-99cafebfe036"],
 "\tUsing the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " function ",
 StyleBox["Transpose",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ",  one can then define the tensor: ",
 StyleBox["gxg",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "=",
 StyleBox["gg-Transpose[gg,{1,3,2,4}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[",",
  FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d28f48f2-e9a2-463e-9260-36fcdd453625"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"244786d7-451d-4aaa-96de-3c8b21578004"],
 "which has components  ",
 StyleBox["gxg[[a,b,c,d]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" = ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["g", "ab"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"0d0726cc-7dbb-49ba-a4a0-48a6481afe47"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["g", 
   RowBox[{"cd", " "}]]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"8401d16f-a151-4eaa-bb49-092c0e72e820"],
 StyleBox["-",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   SubscriptBox["g", "ac"]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"d4ef75f8-a2bb-4bd1-8ba2-a63b51a2a204"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["g", "bd"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"0f11a05d-efc3-4411-8c19-d250b30d5615"],
 ".\n"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"75baf6eb-3e43-45d1-a60a-d25b66f40262"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.3  Contraction of tensor indices", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"f60eec5e-56ea-4898-918b-1bf4a751fe7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSmallCircle]\tThe function  ",
 StyleBox["Contract[x_,{i1_,j1_},{i2_,j2_},..]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  takes as arguments an nth rank tensor ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and one or more lists of  pairs of numbers, indicating the positions of \
the indices to be contracted. It returns a tensor of rank ",
 StyleBox["n-2k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", where ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the number of index-pair lists. ",
 StyleBox["It is assumed that the two numbers in each list refer to one U and \
one d type index, in any order",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  Examples (the Einstein summation convention holds):"
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"8ada4136-3fc1-4de6-8fa4-13a13b9a60ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"bc046fdb-c061-4418-843b-5b4874f761fc"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"574a3824-5d7e-4983-9655-1985674f3471"],
 "\t(a) ",
 StyleBox["Contract[GUdd,{1,3}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  gives a d-type vector with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "ba", "a"],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"6e63f06d-03c3-4025-90e0-d4b5196c51b9"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"5fb3fc67-e161-4f42-bc21-919661cb1910"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"cdb04578-83fc-4bee-aa6d-50068f92665e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"380e034b-255d-4952-8f44-1618cfd1bd5b"],
 "\t(b) ",
 StyleBox["Contract[RUddd,{1,3}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  gives Rdd."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"7e360fa6-3f45-4ed2-982d-450fad317033"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"70d598e0-1e70-4099-aded-4660533feb8b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"51a904c6-257c-49dc-9757-db9bd449c21e"],
 "\t(c) ",
 StyleBox["Contract[Outer[Times,RUddd,RUddd],{1,7},{4,5}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  produces a dddd tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "s"], "abt"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0fede1fb-bb85-489b-82e8-1c6e3dd19b57"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "t"], "csd"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "90d16acc-c916-4345-a61c-4f2667556bfe"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"859dd086-a6a1-4807-9d8c-b736ac2e486a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": Even though the last result can be obtained by calling ",
 StyleBox["Contract",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " twice, each time with a single pair of indices, it is ",
 StyleBox["much",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " more efficient to perform multiple contractions simultaneously, as \
above.",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"282c1532-c516-41ee-a376-c7514b44c390"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"d3cce596-762f-4f2d-a405-5510deaa6d28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note2",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The result of (c) can also be obtained as  ",
 StyleBox["Contract[RUddd.RUddd,{1,5}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", since the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " function ",
 StyleBox["Dot",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " performs the ",
 StyleBox["{4,5}",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " contraction of the outer product (last index of first tensor with first \
index of second tensor) giving a 6th rank tensor.",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"3a701ddf-7eec-407e-b7bf-6345e6dd8e59"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"eabf8842-9fd1-4279-ad9a-7a5e0b8626a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSmallCircle]\tThe function ",
 StyleBox["multiDot[x_,y_,{i1_,j1_},{i2_,j2_},..]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is similar to ",
 StyleBox["Contract",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and generalizes the built-in function ",
 StyleBox["Dot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  It takes as arguments ",
 StyleBox["two",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " tensors -- ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["y",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " -- and one or more lists of  pairs of numbers.  For each pair of numbers \
",
 StyleBox["{i,j}",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", it contracts the ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "th index of the ",
 StyleBox["first",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " tensor (",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ") with the ",
 StyleBox["j",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "th index of the ",
 StyleBox["second",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " tensor (",
 StyleBox["y",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "),  returning a tensor of rank ",
 StyleBox["m+n-2k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", where ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " are the ranks of ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["y",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", respectively, and ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the number of index pairs. Again, it is assumed that the indices at ",
 StyleBox["{i,j}",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " are of opposite (U/d) types. Using ",
 StyleBox["multiDot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", the result of example (c) above can also be obtained as  ",
 StyleBox["multiDot[RUddd,RUddd,{1,3},{4,1}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ".",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["", TextForm]], "",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf42ed04-2451-4742-9bf4-9f38bb17d67c"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["", TextForm]], "",ExpressionUUID->
  "931b1191-162f-4cc0-a498-c55bee3a7c8a"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"c1433082-d37f-4f12-b578-4550fe5d0872"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\tNote1:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " When contracting a product of two tensors, as in example (c), one should \
always use ",
 StyleBox["multiDot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to perform the contractions, thus avoiding the outer product calculation, \
which is very time / memory consuming. See also Example 1a in section 3 and \
Example 4b in Section 5.1",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["", TextForm]], 
  "\.02\[YAcute]\t\[OSlash]\.03\.08\[CapitalCCedilla]`\.03\.08\
\[CapitalCCedilla]`",ExpressionUUID->"8ad3f336-eea0-4630-ad9a-a313b9451888"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"2e30bcb5-c96e-49c8-86fe-58c6f57a6e60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\tNote2:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " One can use ",
 StyleBox["Contract",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["multiDot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to contract nested lists with unequal index dimensions (provided, of \
course, that the indices to be contracted have the same dimension); thus, if \
A has dimensions {2, 3, 3, 4} and B {3, 2, 4}, ",
 StyleBox["Contract",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "[A, {2, 3}] will return a tensor with dimensions {2, 4} and ",
 StyleBox["multiDot",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "[A, B, {1, 2}, {3, 1}] will return a tensor with dimensions {3, 4, 4}.",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["", TextForm]], 
  "\.02\[YAcute]\t\[OSlash]\.03\.08\[CapitalCCedilla]`\.03\.08\
\[CapitalCCedilla]`",ExpressionUUID->"891024b9-54fd-4b6f-9a0d-c0cee504fd5c"]
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"3d2fa420-c2f3-4c54-9c44-2bfa509aac53"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.4  Covariant differentiation of tensors", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"08bf26da-9c5d-441d-a0ac-426b2a1c0aa5"],

Cell["\<\
\tThe following functions, involving differentiations of tensors, are defined \
in RGTC: \
\>", "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"e2e22da1-3418-4930-8e4b-fe0ef75f78ac"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t (i) The function  ",
 StyleBox["covD[x_,{i___}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  takes two arguments -- an nth rank tensor, ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and a list of numbers indicating the positions of the ",
 StyleBox["contravariant",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "  (U) components of ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " -- and produces an ",
 StyleBox["n+1",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " rank tensor: the covariant derivative of ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["The last index is the differentiation index (d type)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". If ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " has only d-type components, the second argument (empty list) can be \
omitted. Examples:"
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"a31f900b-a568-444b-8abd-50aa8869db97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ed9df5c1-5936-4ae4-91c4-52645818f1b9"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"94d3fc21-059d-4108-a905-4e292b9e3be3"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["covD[Rdd]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 3rd rank (ddd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox["R", 
     RowBox[{"ab", ";", "c"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"7425a2bb-eb17-4fd7-b004-06fab6edb6be"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"a66f50f2-fe66-4f2d-b228-4ab07e1f8412"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"2cc0a611-c29b-49a2-bb8c-c087fe94e779"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b0fd4675-bb1b-475b-80cf-6a45511b51c8"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["covD[RUddd,{1}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 5th rank (Udddd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], 
     RowBox[{"bcd", ";", "e"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"24791ff4-bb72-4196-a77b-bda99d62f811"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"b1933f76-e5a6-4d5d-8511-49d0b6b3451b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"4ed5e164-02b6-426c-bb6e-73cc039dc382"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d0c16f2f-af00-45c7-970d-b300f873f3df"],
 "\t(ii) The function ",
 StyleBox["covDiv[x_,{i___,{s_}}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " acting on an nth rank tensor ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with contravariant indices at positions {i..., s} returns an ",
 StyleBox["n-1",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " rank tensor: the covariant ",
 StyleBox["divergence",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with respect to the contravariant index at position ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". If there is only one contravariant index, the second argument can be \
written simply {s} rather than {{s}}. Examples (the Einstein summation \
convention holds):"
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"7820a9a8-932c-47ae-a809-2a828e939880"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"1a1f208a-3719-4c2a-b10e-7fcb8f4d9d1b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8888110b-6a52-4194-8d2c-f424af3034a5"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["covDiv[RUddd,{1}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 3rd rank (ddd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox["R", "s"], 
     RowBox[{"abc", ";", "s"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d90551d1-2bbb-490d-9362-f0b2956165c3"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"a1bceec7-a767-4112-91cf-240095778dfc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"6bab5ffc-9de2-483f-8ef9-f18881bd1400"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"68c575f0-1c05-4e17-947c-c470bfb6928f"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["covDiv[RUdUd,{1,{3}}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 3rd rank (Udd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "b"], "s"], 
     RowBox[{"c", ";", "s"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"2c4874d8-5d12-48ed-8691-396b4edd1319"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"c3774d73-94cf-4614-8617-3fdd31baf72d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e919a294-af4a-4792-8d32-927ea6684784"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"079f06e6-bdb1-4296-ae29-ad7031bc4df7"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": It is ",
 StyleBox["much",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " more efficient to use ",
 StyleBox["covDiv",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  than to use ",
 StyleBox["covD",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  followed by ",
 StyleBox["Contract",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"15da7955-0c93-4dac-9fa2-6167e3abbeee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"4b203626-14da-4b93-839f-87d59be41c87"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"3968acb3-f460-4a07-92e6-8d453c7c6051"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Note2",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The functions ",
 StyleBox["covD",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  and ",
 StyleBox["covDiv",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  can be very slow on high-rank tensors in high dimensions. However, they \
remember their values, so calling them again with the same arguments takes no \
time. "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"95d3bd87-c09e-4625-b991-983f2c00a476"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t(iii)  The function  ",
 StyleBox["LieD[h_,x_,{i___}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " computes the Lie derivative of the tensor ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", having contravariant indices at index positions ",
 StyleBox["i__",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", with respect to the contravariant (U type) vector ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The tensor ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " can be a tensor-valued p-form, for example the curvature 2-form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "b"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0a798b67-9855-4747-9845-a4d92caa767c"],
 "=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "bcd"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2d81e89f-f125-4579-b9aa-3140a32b2bd8"],
 "d[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["x", "c"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d46987f0-800b-4595-8180-923dc46d4710"],
 "]\[Wedge]d[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["x", "d"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e227ea5f-1412-4bf4-a0b7-83ad519e0c5b"],
 "]. For totally covariant tensors ",
 StyleBox["x ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(or scalars), the last argument (empty list) can be omitted. The result of ",
 StyleBox["LieD",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a tensor of the same rank (and type) as ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". As with ",
 StyleBox["covD",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "  and ",
 StyleBox["covDiv",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ",  ",
 StyleBox["LieD",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " remembers its values. Examples:"
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"0bf673b3-36cc-4bd2-99a1-a3e5a8171415"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"bcfe2806-2137-4c7c-ade7-14a2a14f11a2"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"8136f053-bd60-4212-a1cd-32f27832613c"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["LieD[{h1,h2,..,hn},gdd]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 2nd rank (dd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    TagBox["",
     DisplayForm], 
    SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"ab", ",", "s"}]]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    TagBox[
     TagBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
       RowBox[{",", "a"}]],
      DisplayForm],
     DisplayForm], 
    SubscriptBox["g", "sb"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    TagBox[
     TagBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
       RowBox[{",", "b"}]],
      DisplayForm],
     DisplayForm], 
    SubscriptBox["g", "as"]}]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "026a43ee-a6cf-4ee6-a727-1e64c4907c9c"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"c09563a3-175c-44b4-a6c1-03698228b4f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"e4636432-4b5c-4e54-b746-c9fc2aac9321"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"bd11c54d-0596-4de2-b34a-acbad4e7cb5c"],
 "\t     ",
 StyleBox["LieD[{h1,h2,..,hn},RUddd,{1}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a 4th rank (Uddd type) tensor with components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], 
      RowBox[{"bcd", ",", "s"}]]}],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"756942f1-ed64-4fcc-a12b-73be11569b67"],
 "+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
     RowBox[{",", "b"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d85b35b6-559f-452e-9052-4ff75568a684"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "scd"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d2fc8c57-fd2b-45b0-b661-51cd7dce6dd2"],
 "+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TagBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
      RowBox[{",", "c"}]],
     DisplayForm],
    DisplayForm], 
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "bsd"]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "45c14e16-6c76-4065-b571-75ab08e0949b"],
 "+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     SuperscriptBox["h", "s"], 
     RowBox[{",", "d"}]],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"dcf03f67-b156-4578-929a-9b0be20bc802"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "a"], "bcs"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f5392eb7-9d07-46ae-ad44-006a8f86c435"],
 StyleBox["- ",
  FontFamily->"Geneva"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["h", "a"], 
      RowBox[{",", "s"}]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      SuperscriptBox["R", "s"], "bcd"]}],
    DisplayForm],
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"1621e533-d8cc-49ec-a9f0-fb56e7044daa"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"7ebdcda5-073b-4da0-9913-eed447bf297b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tThe function  ",
 StyleBox["LieDcartan",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["[",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["vector_,form_",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", introduced in ",
 ButtonBox["EDC 3.8.5",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData:>{
    URL["http://www.inp.demokritos.gr/~sbonano/EDC/"], None}],
 ", computes the Lie derivative of the differential form expression ",
 StyleBox["form",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " w.r.t. the ",
 StyleBox["vector",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " using the Cartan identity.  It differs from ",
 StyleBox["LieD",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " in that it does not treat lists of forms as components of a tensor. See \
the ",
 ButtonBox["EDCmanual.nb",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData:>{
    URL["http://www.inp.demokritos.gr/~sbonano/EDC/"], None}],
 " (section 2.5) for details."
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"e9ae95a4-e0e7-4ffb-81ce-3f2d062b2ebe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t(iv) The function  ",
 StyleBox["Laplacian[x_,{i___}]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " computes the Laplacian (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"=", "x"}], 
    RowBox[{";", "s"}]], 
   RowBox[{";", "s"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5a3daaab-184b-4cf6-81a1-cf10a1703797"],
 ") of the tensor ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", having contravariant indices at index positions ",
 StyleBox["i__",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". Again, for totally covariant tensors ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (or scalars), the last argument (empty list) can be omitted. The result of \
",
 StyleBox["Laplacian",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a tensor of the same rank (and type) as ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"20aced06-5c1a-4b6d-8c46-5ee843d661b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t(v) The function  ",
 StyleBox["Grad2Norm[x__]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " takes either 1 or 2  ",
 StyleBox["scalar",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " functions as arguments and computes the square norm of the gradient of ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (inner product): ",
 StyleBox["Grad2Norm[x]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "= ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["g", "ab"], 
   SubscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{",", "a"}]], 
   SubscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{",", "b"}]]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dc19cd54-508b-429a-90c9-2b7b804711a7"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "and  ",
 StyleBox["Grad2Norm[x,y]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "= ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["g", "ab"], 
   SubscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{",", "a"}]], 
   SubscriptBox["y", 
    RowBox[{",", "b"}]]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "88fe5beb-1fa7-4dfa-8701-8c904c5c80d7"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"a6b7f3a8-ba90-45cf-806d-a5ebc95a9615"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ed2f73e9-1a9a-458f-bc84-52ace41f23ad"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"fee0b6bc-ae7e-4aa1-9b13-ec01d3ac4875"],
 "\t(vi) Using ",
 StyleBox["covD",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["covDiv",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ",  the function ",
 StyleBox["Bianchi[n_]",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", for n = 0, 1, 2, computes the full, once, twice contracted Bianchi \
identities and returns a list containing any non-vanishing terms. This list \
is normally the empty list, except when the simplification rules used imply \
relations among the 3rd derivatives of the metric functions (see Example 5). \
"
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"f39e662e-6c23-45cc-b88d-f6b94c24dda1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tEvaluation of the Bianchi Identities takes long: for the metrics in the \
examples, the time needed to evaluate ",
 StyleBox["Bianchi[1]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is ~ 1 - 15 times the time taken by ",
 StyleBox["RGtensors",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to compute all basic tensors. ",
 StyleBox["Bianchi[0]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " takes considerably longer. (For the Bondi metric the times are ~ 12 min, 6 \
min, 7 sec). "
}], "Text",
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"4ad6d70a-4fd4-4ddb-8ff9-5c9eeb52f2da"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.5  Index of global names / variables", "Subsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"b3fc218f-744e-458a-bd02-e2905241cb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["It is essential that, in choosing coordinates and metric \
functions, one avoids using the symbols listed in this subsection, as they \
are defined by (or have special meanings in) RGTC. In particular, the  \
single-letter symbols R, d, e, as well as the greek letters used in the spin \
coefficient formalism, must be avoided-- see subsection 4.0.",
  FontSize->16]
}], "Text",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0, 0, 1],ExpressionUUID->"109c1e99-f680-430d-aafe-974131b206be"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"9e4845a0-2bc3-45aa-b076-6e13ad9095cf"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox["",
   DisplayForm]],ExpressionUUID->"16732e85-c4ec-4369-99bb-74868999bf1f"],
 "\t(i) ",
 StyleBox["Riemannian Geometry tensors / scalars",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " "
}], "Subsubsection",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 FontSize->16,ExpressionUUID->"fbe4dd2f-1b43-4d96-a70f-76b5e61e5e1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\t",
 StyleBox["gdd, gUU, GUdd, Rdddd, RUddd, Rdd, EUd, R, Wdddd, detg\t\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(section 1.1)\n\t",
 StyleBox["epsilon, eta\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(section 1.1.1)\n\t",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]Ud \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(section 5.1)\n\t",
 StyleBox["\[Alpha],\[Beta],",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["...,  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
